CREATE OR REPLACE PROCEDURE sp(para_activity_name text, para_actid integer, para_LName text, para_Fname text) LANGUAGE plpgsql AS $$ DECLARE
  ref_cursor1 CURSOR FOR SELECT * FROM "Participates_in" WHERE "actid" = para_actid FOR UPDATE;
  ref_cursor2 CURSOR FOR SELECT * FROM "Student" FOR UPDATE;
  rec1 RECORD;
  rec2 RECORD;
BEGIN
  UPDATE "Activity" SET "activity_name" = {SLOT_1};
  UPDATE "Faculty"
    SET "Rank" = {SLOT_2}
    WHERE {SLOT_3};
  DELETE FROM "Faculty_Participates_in" WHERE {SLOT_4};
  OPEN ref_cursor1;
  LOOP
    FETCH ref_cursor1 INTO rec1;
    EXIT WHEN NOT FOUND;
    DELETE FROM "Participates_in" WHERE CURRENT OF ref_cursor1;
  END LOOP;
  CLOSE ref_cursor1;
  OPEN ref_cursor2;
  LOOP
    FETCH ref_cursor2 INTO rec2;
    EXIT WHEN NOT FOUND;
    UPDATE "Student" SET "LName" = {SLOT_5}, "Fname" = {SLOT_6} WHERE CURRENT OF ref_cursor2;
  END LOOP;
  CLOSE ref_cursor2;
END; $$;

## Slots

### {SLOT_1}
- Kind: value
- What must go there: the procedure input parameter named `para_activity_name`. It is a text value and is assigned to the `Activity.activity_name` column for every row. No transformation or filtering is involved in this slot; it supplies the new value only.

### {SLOT_2}
- Kind: value
- What must go there: the literal text string `Professor` with exactly that spelling and capitalization. It is a text literal assigned to `Faculty.Rank`, not a column or parameter reference.

### {SLOT_3}
- Kind: predicate
- What must go there: a membership predicate for the `Faculty` update. A `Faculty` row qualifies when its `FacID` column is exactly one of the `FacID` values found in the `Faculty_Participates_in` table among rows whose `actid` column is exactly equal to the procedure parameter `para_actid`. The comparison between `Faculty_Participates_in.actid` and `para_actid` uses exact equality, not any other comparison. The membership test applies to `Faculty.FacID` against that set of `Faculty_Participates_in.FacID` values.

### {SLOT_4}
- Kind: predicate
- What must go there: the deletion condition for `Faculty_Participates_in`. A row qualifies when its `actid` column is exactly equal to the procedure parameter `para_actid`. Use exact equality and no other row-selection condition.

### {SLOT_5}
- Kind: value
- What must go there: the procedure input parameter named `para_LName`. It is a text value and is assigned unchanged to the `Student.LName` column for each row reached in the locked `Student` traversal.

### {SLOT_6}
- Kind: value
- What must go there: the procedure input parameter named `para_Fname`. It is a text value and is assigned unchanged to the `Student.Fname` column for each row reached in the locked `Student` traversal.

